{"The spans.buffer.flusher.wait_produce metric uses tag key 'shards' (plural) while all other metrics in the same function use 'shard' (singular), preventing consistent tag-based correlation in dashboards and alerts.": 0.8410369157791138, "In join(), when the deadline expires during process iteration, break exits the loop without terminating remaining processes. Processes not yet visited in the loop never have terminate() called, allowing them to continue producing to Kafka after the consumer considers shutdown complete.": 0.9425563216209412, "SpanFlusher derives num_processes directly from max_processes without enforcing it is >= 1; a negative value will make i % self.num_processes raise at startup, preventing any flushing. The CLI option also accepts negative integers (type=int), so this can be triggered by configuration.": 0.8970730304718018, "When produce_to_pipe is set, workers run as threads, but the unhealthy-restart path only kills multiprocessing.Process instances before spawning replacements. This can leave the old thread running while a new one starts for the same shards, causing duplicate flush/produce and unbounded thread leaks.": 0.9147087931632996}